---
const run = "battistics run --name Build -- swift build";
const runLid = "battistics run --minutes 120 --mode lidClosed -- ./export.sh";
const mcp = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "battistics": {
      "command": "/Applications/Battistics.app/Contents/MacOS/battistics-mcp",
      "args": []
    }
  }
}`;
---

<section class="dev" id="developers" aria-labelledby="dev-title">
  <h2 id="dev-title">Long builds and AI tasks keep the Mac up by themselves</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Turn on Local automation in Power. Keep Awake then lasts exactly as long as a command, or from the start to the end
    of an AI task. It never kills your command, and nothing leaves the Mac: no port, no API key.
  </p>
  <div class="pair">
    <article class="card">
      <header>
        <h3>Terminal</h3>
        <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={run}>Copy</button>
      </header>
      <pre><code><span class="comment"># Awake for as long as the build runs</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> {run}

<span class="comment"># Two hours at most, lid closed in a bag</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> {runLid}</code></pre>
      <ul>
        <li>Runs in your shell, with your directory, environment and output.</li>
        <li>Ends when the command does, 12 hours at most.</li>
        <li>Exit status is the command's own.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/docs/automation/terminal/">Terminal guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <header>
        <h3>MCP for AI clients</h3>
        <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={mcp}>Copy</button>
      </header>
      <pre><code set:html={mcp.replace(/("[^"]*")(\s*:)/g, '<span class="key">$1</span>$2').replace(/(:\s*)("[^"]*")/g, '$1<span class="str">$2</span>')} /></pre>
      <ul>
        <li>The client calls start before the work and stop after it.</li>
        <li>A stalled or closed client ends its session within 45 seconds.</li>
        <li>It cannot touch protection settings or anything else.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/docs/automation/mcp/">MCP guide</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .dev { max-width: var(--page); margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(80px, 12vw, 140px) var(--gutter) 0; }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 20ch;
    font: 720 clamp(2.1rem, 4.2vw, 3.3rem) / 1 var(--display);
    font-stretch: 86%;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede { max-width: 64ch; margin: 20px 0 0; font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 18px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: #121916;
    color: #e3ebe6;
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.06);
  }
  .card header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
  .card h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; }
  .copy {
    width: 74px;
    height: 30px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font: 600 13px var(--text);
    color: #e3ebe6;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .copy:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent-a); outline-offset: 2px; }
  pre {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 200px;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 16px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #0a0f0d;
    font: 13px/1.65 var(--mono);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .comment { color: #6f8279; }
  .prompt { color: var(--accent-a); user-select: none; }
  pre :global(.key) { color: #8fd3c7; }
  pre :global(.str) { color: #d8e88f; }
  .card ul { margin: 16px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; color: #a9b8b0; line-height: 1.5; }
  .card a { margin-top: 14px; color: var(--accent-a); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    pre { min-height: 0; }
  }
</style>
